meta { name: Onboard an author into a site, type: http, seq: 3 }
post { url: {{adminBase}}/platform/tenants/{{tenantId}}/authors, body: json, auth: none }
headers { Cookie: {{sessionCookie}} }
body:json {
  {
    "username": "tomas-reyes",
    "name": "Tomas Reyes",
    "email": "tomas@example.com",
    "role": "admin"
  }
}
docs {
  Bootstraps a site's first admin. Same use case as POST /admin/v1/authors —
  only the tenant source differs (path, not session).

  The returned invite.link is shown ONCE and is not stored. There is no endpoint
  that returns it again.

  A3 revised 2026-11-10: platform admins onboard; they do NOT edit or
  deactivate. Those stay with the site's own admins.
}
